    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><p>Much like the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Corellian_Powersuit\" title=\"Corellian Powersuit\">Corellian Powersuit</a>, other Armors can be Upgraded to include a Powered Exoskeleton that enhances the physical strength of the wearer. Because of the weight and energy required, only a suit of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medium_Armor\" title=\"Medium Armor\">Medium Armor</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Armor\" title=\"Heavy Armor\">Heavy Armor</a> can have the Powered Exoskeleton Upgrade. </p><p>A Powered Exoskeleton operates for 20 rounds on a standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a>. (Suits of Armor with a Powered Exoskeleton commonly have the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Internal_Generator\" title=\"Internal Generator\">Internal Generator</a> Upgrade.) Turning a Powered Exoskeleton on or off is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>. When active, the Powered Exoskeleton gives the wearer a +2 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> bonus to their <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> score. A Powered Exoskeleton adds 5 kg to the weight of the Armor. </p>",
